        "id": "p38-q5-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}3x+2y&=7\\\\5x+y&=7\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=1,\\ y=2$",
          "worked": "Multiply the second equation by 2, then subtract the first equation.\n$$\\begin{align*}10x+2y&=14\\\\(10x+2y)-(3x+2y)&=14-7\\\\7x&=7\\\\x&=1\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute into the second equation.\n$$\\begin{align*}5(1)+y&=7\\\\y&=2\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $x=1,\\ y=2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q5-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}3x+2y&=0\\\\2x-y&=56\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=16,\\ y=-24$",
          "worked": "Multiply the second equation by 2, then add the first equation.\n$$\\begin{align*}4x-2y&=112\\\\(3x+2y)+(4x-2y)&=112\\\\7x&=112\\\\x&=16\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute into the second equation.\n$$\\begin{align*}2(16)-y&=56\\\\-y&=24\\\\y&=-24\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $x=16,\\ y=-24$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q5-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}5m+4n&=22\\\\m-5n&=-13\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$m=2,\\ n=3$",
          "worked": "Multiply the second equation by 5, then subtract it from the first equation.\n$$\\begin{align*}5m-25n&=-65\\\\(5m+4n)-(5m-25n)&=22-(-65)\\\\29n&=87\\\\n&=3\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute into the second equation.\n$$\\begin{align*}m-5(3)&=-13\\\\m-15&=-13\\\\m&=2\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $m=2,\\ n=3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 72
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q5-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}15x+2y&=27\\\\3x+7y&=45\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=1,\\ y=6$",
          "worked": "Multiply the second equation by 5, then subtract the first equation.\n$$\\begin{align*}15x+35y&=225\\\\(15x+35y)-(15x+2y)&=225-27\\\\33y&=198\\\\y&=6\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute into the second equation.\n$$\\begin{align*}3x+7(6)&=45\\\\3x+42&=45\\\\3x&=3\\\\x&=1\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $x=1,\\ y=6$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 72
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q5-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}3a-4b&=-16\\\\2a+3b&=12\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=0,\\ b=4$",
          "worked": "Multiply the first equation by 2 and the second by 3, then subtract.\n$$\\begin{align*}6a-8b&=-32\\\\6a+9b&=36\\\\(6a+9b)-(6a-8b)&=36-(-32)\\\\17b&=68\\\\b&=4\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute into the second equation.\n$$\\begin{align*}2a+3(4)&=12\\\\2a+12&=12\\\\2a&=0\\\\a&=0\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $a=0,\\ b=4$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 80
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q5-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}3x-2y&=11\\\\4x+3y&=43\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=7,\\ y=5$",
          "worked": "Multiply the first equation by 3 and the second by 2, then add.\n$$\\begin{align*}9x-6y&=33\\\\8x+6y&=86\\\\(9x-6y)+(8x+6y)&=33+86\\\\17x&=119\\\\x&=7\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute into the first equation.\n$$\\begin{align*}3(7)-2y&=11\\\\21-2y&=11\\\\-2y&=-10\\\\y&=5\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $x=7,\\ y=5$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 80
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q5-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}2x+3y&=28\\\\3x+2y&=27\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=5,\\ y=6$",
          "worked": "Multiply the first equation by 3 and the second by 2, then subtract.\n$$\\begin{align*}6x+9y&=84\\\\6x+4y&=54\\\\(6x+9y)-(6x+4y)&=84-54\\\\5y&=30\\\\y&=6\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute into the first equation.\n$$\\begin{align*}2x+3(6)&=28\\\\2x+18&=28\\\\2x&=10\\\\x&=5\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $x=5,\\ y=6$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 80
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q5-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}5p+2q+17&=0\\\\2p-3q+11&=0\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$p=-\\dfrac{73}{19},\\ q=\\dfrac{21}{19}$",
          "worked": "Rearrange both equations. Multiply the first by 3 and the second by 2, then add.\n$$\\begin{align*}5p+2q&=-17\\\\2p-3q&=-11\\\\15p+6q&=-51\\\\4p-6q&=-22\\\\(15p+6q)+(4p-6q)&=-51-22\\\\19p&=-73\\\\p&=-\\frac{73}{19}\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute into the first equation.\n$$\\begin{align*}5\\left(-\\frac{73}{19}\\right)+2q&=-17\\\\2q&=-\\frac{323}{19}+\\frac{365}{19}\\\\2q&=\\frac{42}{19}\\\\q&=\\frac{21}{19}\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $p=-\\dfrac{73}{19},\\ q=\\dfrac{21}{19}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 100
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q5-i",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "i",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}-2h+3k&=-14\\\\2k&=5h-13\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$h=1,\\ k=-4$",
          "worked": "Rearrange the second equation. Multiply the first by 5 and the rearranged second equation by 2, then add.\n$$\\begin{align*}5h-2k&=13\\\\-10h+15k&=-70\\\\10h-4k&=26\\\\(-10h+15k)+(10h-4k)&=-70+26\\\\11k&=-44\\\\k&=-4\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute into the first equation.\n$$\\begin{align*}-2h+3(-4)&=-14\\\\-2h-12&=-14\\\\-2h&=-2\\\\h&=1\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $h=1,\\ k=-4$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 88
      }
